      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "StimmaToolInfo"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "fish-audio-drama-3-dialogue",
        "Fish Audio Drama 3 Dialogue",
        "text-to-speech",
        "",
        "Generate a two-speaker conversation locally from a script and two voice references. References are transcribed automatically, and each speaker retains their own voice context.",
        "Fish Audio",
        "Drama 3",
        "The prompt is the exact text to speak. Place cues such as [sighs], [laughs], or [whispers] where they should happen; parentheses are spoken aloud. Long text is split automatically. If a take becomes silent or skips words, retry with another seed or a different reference. Supply exactly two clean voice references in input_audios: item 1 is speaker 0, item 2 is speaker 1. Start every script line with <|speaker:0|> or <|speaker:1|>. Each reference should be a few seconds of one speaker, cut between sentences. The per-chunk generation limit can truncate slow or very long speech; it is not a target duration. Check that the full script was spoken."
      ]
    },
